      {
        "id": "lem-step-up-leave-one-out-rejection-partition",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "deps": [
          "def-borel-sigma-algebra",
          "def-measurable-function-between-measurable-spaces",
          "def-product-sigma-algebra-and-finite-product-sigma-algebras",
          "thm-seven-generators-of-the-borel-sigma-algebra-on-r"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "title": "Leave-one-coordinate rejection partition for a step-up rule",
        "justified_by": [],
        "statement": "Let $m\\ge1$, $p=(p_1,\\ldots,p_m)\\in[0,1]^m$, and critical values $0<c_1\\le\\cdots\\le c_m\\le1$. Give $[0,1]^m$ its finite product of the trace Borel sigma-algebras on $[0,1]$. Define the step-up rule by\n\n$$R:=\\max\\bigl(\\{k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}:p_{(k)}\\le c_k\\}\\cup\\{0\\}\\bigr),$$\n\nrejecting exactly ranks $1,\\ldots,R$. Fix $i\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$. Give the remaining-coordinate space $[0,1]^{m-1}$ its finite product of the trace Borel sigma-algebras, with the empty product on the singleton empty tuple when $m=1$. Write the remaining values in increasing order as $y_{(1)}\\le\\cdots\\le y_{(m-1)}$, and set $y_{(0)}=0$. For $1\\le k\\le m$, let\n\n$$C_{i,k}:=\\{y_{(k-1)}\\le c_k\\}\\cap\\bigcap_{r=k}^{m-1}\\{y_{(r)}>c_{r+1}\\},$$\n\nwith an empty intersection interpreted as the whole remaining-coordinate space. Put $D_{i,k}:=\\bigcup_{j=1}^k C_{i,j}$. For $x\\in[0,1]^m$, let $I_i(x)=1$ if the rule rejects coordinate $i$, and $I_i(x)=0$ otherwise. Then:\n\n1. For every $k$, the following identity of subsets of $[0,1]^m$ holds:\n   $$\\{x\\in[0,1]^m:I_i(x)=1,\\ R(x)=k\\}=\\{x\\in[0,1]^m:x_i\\le c_k\\}\\cap\\{x\\in[0,1]^m:x_{-i}\\in C_{i,k}\\}.$$\n   In particular, every input in the right-hand side has exactly $k$ rejections and rejects $i$.\n2. The sets $C_{i,1},\\ldots,C_{i,m}$ are a disjoint Borel partition of $[0,1]^{m-1}$.\n3. For $k<m$,\n   $$D_{i,k}=\\bigcap_{r=k}^{m-1}\\{y_{(r)}>c_{r+1}\\},$$\n   and $D_{i,m}$ is the whole space. Each $D_{i,k}$ is a coordinatewise increasing Borel set.\n\nFor $m=1$, the remaining-coordinate space is the singleton empty tuple with its full sigma-algebra, and $C_{i,1}=D_{i,1}$ is the whole space."
      },
